   - **`new Date()`**: Returns the current date and time in JavaScript format.
   - **`res`**: Represents the response object from the server.
   - **`next()`**: Continues processing the request with the next middleware or handler in the chain.

This setup allows for simple and efficient logging of incoming HTTP requests and responses within a NestJS application.

To create a multi-tree list (also known as a hierarchical tree structure) within an Angular application that can be used as a text editor, you need to follow several steps:

### Step 1: Set up the Project

First, make sure you have Angular CLI installed and initialized your project.

```bash
npm install -g @angular/cli
ng new my-text-editor-app
cd my-text-editor-app
```

### Step 2: Create the Tree Structure

We'll use `@types/node` for our JSON data model. First, generate a basic CRUD service to interact with this data.

```bash
ng generate service treeservice --flat
```

This will create a file named `treeservice.ts`.

### Step 3: Define the Tree Data Model

In your `treeservice.ts`, define the structure of the tree nodes. For simplicity, we'll assume each node has an ID, label, children, and some additional properties like `isLeaf` or `isExpanded`.

```typescript
export interface TreeNode {
  id: string;
  label: string;
  isLeaf?: boolean; // Optional property indicating if it's a leaf node
  expanded?: boolean; // Optional property indicating if the subtree is expanded
  children?: TreeNode[];
}
```

### Step 4: Implement Multi-Tree List Component

Now, let's create the component where the user will see the tree view and edit its content.

#### `tree.component.html`

```html
<div class="tree">
  <ul>
    <!-- This template uses ngFor and should be replaced with actual logic -->
    <li *ngFor="let node of treeData" [id]="node.id" [label]="node.label">
      <button mat-raised-button color="primary" (click)="toggle(node)">Toggle</button>
      <div class="content">{{ node.content }}</div>
    </li>
  </ul>
</div>

<button mat-raised-button color="warn" (click)="addNode()">Add Node</button>
<button mat-raised-button color="success" (click)="removeSelectedNodes()">Remove Selected Nodes</button>
```

